---
const DEMO_URL = "https://motorshop-sepia-omega.vercel.app/";
const REPO_URL = "https://github.com/lukahristic/motor-shop";

const signals = [
  {
    label: "Fitment is a relationship, not a field",
    detail:
      "A part doesn't belong to one bike — it fits many, and each bike takes many parts. That's a join table, not a column. Year, Make, and Model chain into each other, and the results only show parts that actually fit.",
  },
  {
    label: "Auth written by hand, on purpose",
    detail:
      "bcrypt for hashing, JWT in an HTTP-only cookie so JavaScript can't read it. I skipped the drop-in auth library because I wanted to understand the session, not configure one.",
  },
  {
    label: "Wrong email and wrong password say the same thing",
    detail:
      "Different error messages let anyone check which emails have accounts. One message for both, so the login form doesn't leak the user list.",
  },
  {
    label: "Guards at the middleware, not the UI",
    detail:
      "Admin routes and mutation endpoints are blocked before they render. Hiding a button is not access control — the check has to sit where the request arrives.",
  },
];
---

<section id="ecommerce" class="bg-paper-mid border-t border-paper-dark">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-24">

    <!-- Header -->
    <div data-reveal class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-16">
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-ink-muted uppercase tracking-widest">Case Study 02</p>
      <span class="flex-1 border-t border-paper-dark"></span>
      <span class="font-body text-xs text-ink-muted uppercase tracking-wider">Technical Credibility</span>
    </div>

    <h2 data-reveal class="font-display text-5xl md:text-6xl font-light text-ink mb-4" style="line-height: var(--leading-tight);">
      MotorShop
    </h2>
    <p data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1" class="font-display text-2xl font-light text-ink-muted mb-16" style="font-style: italic;">
      A parts store has to know what fits what.
    </p>

    <!-- Live demo — the whole point -->
    <div
      data-reveal
      class="mb-16 border border-paper-dark rounded-lg overflow-hidden"
      style="border-left-width: 3px; border-left-color: var(--color-accent);"
    >
      <div class="px-6 py-6">
        <p class="font-body text-xs text-ink-faint uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">
          Running right now
        </p>
        <p class="font-body text-base text-ink mb-5" style="line-height: var(--leading-normal);">
          Don't take my word for any of this — sign in as an administrator and look around.
        </p>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2 mb-5">
          <a
            href={DEMO_URL}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="font-body text-sm text-accent hover:text-accent-warm transition-colors"
          >
            Open the live store →
          </a>
          <a
            href={REPO_URL}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="font-body text-sm text-accent hover:text-accent-warm transition-colors"
          >
            Read the source →
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="pt-4 border-t border-paper-dark">
          <p class="font-body text-xs text-ink-faint uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">
            Demo accounts
          </p>
          <dl class="font-body text-sm text-ink-muted flex flex-wrap gap-x-10 gap-y-2">
            <div>
              <dt class="text-ink-faint text-xs mb-0.5">Admin</dt>
              <dd>admin@motorshop.com · password123</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-ink-faint text-xs mb-0.5">Customer</dt>
              <dd>user@motorshop.com · password123</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Framing -->
    <div data-reveal class="mb-16">
      <p class="font-body text-lg text-ink mb-6" style="line-height: var(--leading-loose);">
        Most shop tutorials treat a product as a thing with a price. A motorcycle
        parts store can't. A brake lever fits some bikes and not others, and
        selling someone a part that doesn't fit their machine is the one mistake
        the whole store exists to prevent.
      </p>

      <p class="font-body text-lg text-ink mb-6" style="line-height: var(--leading-loose);">
        So the interesting work wasn't the checkout. It was the modelling —
        and then building the boring parts correctly around it: real
        authentication, real access control, a database that runs the same
        locally as it does in production.
      </p>

      <p class="font-body text-lg text-ink" style="line-height: var(--leading-loose);">
        To be clear about what this is: nobody uses it. It has no customers and
        was never meant to — it's the project where I worked out how the pieces
        fit together. The store is pretend. The authentication, the access
        control, and the data model are not, and those are the parts I'd defend
        in a review.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Engineering signals -->
    <div class="mb-16">
      <p data-reveal class="font-body text-xs text-ink-faint uppercase tracking-widest mb-8">The decisions worth defending</p>

      <div class="grid gap-px bg-paper-dark border border-paper-dark rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {signals.map((s, i) => (
          <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay={i + 1} class="bg-paper-mid p-6">
            <p class="font-body text-sm font-semibold text-ink mb-1">{s.label}</p>
            <p class="font-body text-sm text-ink-muted" style="line-height: var(--leading-normal);">{s.detail}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Environment parity -->
    <div data-reveal class="mb-16">
      <p class="font-body text-lg text-ink" style="line-height: var(--leading-loose);">
        Local development runs Postgres in Docker; production runs it on Neon.
        Same engine, same migrations, one Prisma schema — so "works on my machine"
        stops being a category of bug. That was a cost decision as much as a
        technical one: managed Postgres for a portfolio project is worth the
        money, self-hosting it isn't.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Stack + status -->
    <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-end justify-between gap-6 pt-8 border-t border-paper-dark">
      <div>
        <p class="font-body text-xs text-ink-faint uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">Stack</p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          {["Next.js 15", "TypeScript", "Prisma", "Postgres", "Docker", "Vercel"].map((tech) => (
            <span class="font-body text-xs text-ink-muted border border-paper-dark px-2 py-1 rounded">
              {tech}
            </span>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="font-body text-xs text-ink-muted uppercase tracking-wider bg-paper-dark px-3 py-1 rounded-full">
          Live demo
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
